  "body": "Follow-up from #4031 (the maintainer scoped steps 1, 2 and 5 there; this is the rest).\n\nWhat happens: a tool can now state `cutter_hand: left` (step 1), and the tool gate refuses it on the M3-only posts (step 2). But no operation reads the hand yet, so on a post that reverses (Fanuc, Mazak, Mach4, Siemens 810M) a left-hand cutter still posts M3.\n\nDone means:\n- Step 3: the operations that turn a cutter read the tool's `cutter_hand` and mark their stream (`ask_reverse_spindle`, the #988 `MillSpindle reverse` PARAM) for a left-hand tool.\n- Step 4: a posted program shows M4 for a left-hand cutter and M3 for a right-hand one, on every post that declares `millSpindleReverse`; a post without the flag keeps the #988 refusal by name.\n\nPinned by posted-G-code tests: fanuc.cps writes M4 for a left-hand drill and M3 for a right-hand one.\n\nRefs #4031.\n",
